From dcfe97286ed249d80755e28105bf4efebffea163 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(nxs-pack): unit tests for the host-side helpers

nxs-pack had no tests (its header said so). Add a #[cfg(test)] module in
src/tests.rs, kept out of main.rs so the file stays well under the
structure-gate's 600-line limit, for the pure helpers named in #47:

- parse_args: every flag in any order, each missing flag, a flag without
  a value, an unknown argument. The parser now takes its argument list
  as an iterator (parse_args_from) so a test can drive it; the binary
  still reads env::args.
- parse_meta / req_str / opt_u64: version trimmed, a missing timestamp
  defaulting to 0, a missing or non-string system_version, a blank one,
  a negative or non-integer timestamp, invalid TOML, a missing file.
- parse_manifest: name and semver read and trimmed, a blank name or
  semver, bytes that are not a Cap'n Proto message.
- read_file_with_limit: a file at the limit is read, one byte over is
  refused, a missing file is an error.
- sha256: the known digests of "" and "abc" (the FIPS 180-2 example).

Rejection tests use the test_reject_* naming. tempfile is a new
dev-dependency (already in the lockfile, used the same way by nxb-pack).
The archive format is unchanged. The header's TEST_COVERAGE line now
points at the tests.

Closes #47
